# 4. Non-Goals

The following are explicitly **out of scope** for this product. Each is accompanied by a justification.

| ID | Non-Goal | Justification |
|---|---|---|
| NG-01 | Hiding the application from screen recording or screen sharing | Violates transparency principle; would associate the product with cheating tools |
| NG-02 | Bypassing browser or application security mechanisms | Illegal in many jurisdictions; violates CFAA, DMCA, and equivalents |
| NG-03 | Circumventing online examination or proctoring systems | Directly unethical; would expose users and the company to legal liability |
| NG-04 | Evading anti-cheat or detection systems | Same as above |
| NG-05 | Impersonating Windows system processes | Malware behavior; would trigger antivirus flags and destroy user trust |
| NG-06 | Injecting code into, hooking, or manipulating memory of other processes | Requires admin privileges; malware behavior |
| NG-07 | Requiring administrator privileges for normal operation | Reduces portability and increases security risk |
| NG-08 | Installing drivers or kernel components | Incompatible with portability; requires admin; introduces stability risk |
| NG-09 | Modifying Windows registry or system internals | Incompatible with portability; requires elevated privileges |
| NG-10 | Cloud synchronization (v1) | Deferred to future roadmap to limit v1 scope and keep data local |
| NG-11 | Mobile or macOS/Linux support (v1) | Windows-first; cross-platform deferred to future roadmap |
| NG-12 | Plugin/extension system (v1) | Architecture will be plugin-ready, but the runtime and API are deferred |
| NG-13 | Real-time collaboration | Out of scope for a local-only tool |
| NG-14 | AI-powered features (summarization, auto-complete) | Users access AI through the embedded browser; the host app does not add its own AI layer |
| NG-15 | Privilege escalation of any kind | Security non-negotiable |

