## 7.1 Module 1: Application Core

### Purpose
Provide the foundational runtime, lifecycle management, and portability infrastructure.

| Req ID | Requirement | Priority | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|---|---|
| FR-AC-01 | The application MUST be distributed as a portable, self-contained folder (no installer) | P0 | Copy folder to a new machine → application launches without installation |
| FR-AC-02 | The application MUST run on Windows 10 version 1809 and later, and Windows 11 | P0 | Tested on Windows 10 1809, 21H2, and Windows 11 23H2 |
| FR-AC-03 | The application MUST NOT require administrator privileges for normal operation | P0 | Runs under a standard user account; no UAC prompt |
| FR-AC-04 | The application MUST start within 5 seconds on a machine with an SSD and 8 GB RAM | P0 | Measured from process start to interactive UI |
| FR-AC-05 | Idle RAM usage MUST be below 200 MB (excluding browser tab content) | P0 | Measured with 0 tabs open, idle for 60 s |
| FR-AC-06 | Idle CPU usage MUST be below 2% | P0 | Measured with 0 tabs open, idle for 60 s |
| FR-AC-07 | The application MUST store all user data in a `data/` subdirectory relative to the executable | P0 | No writes to AppData, registry, or temp unless OS-mandated (e.g., Chromium cache) |
| FR-AC-08 | The application MUST support running multiple instances simultaneously | P2 | Each instance operates independently; no port conflicts |
| FR-AC-09 | The application MUST display a splash screen during initialization | P1 | Splash shows logo, version, and loading progress |
| FR-AC-10 | The application MUST expose a `--version` CLI argument | P1 | Prints version string and exits |
| FR-AC-11 | The application MUST use a single-threaded main event loop with offloaded blocking operations | P0 | UI never freezes for > 100 ms |

### Design Rationale
Portability is a core differentiator. Storing all data relative to the executable enables USB-stick deployment and avoids polluting the host system. The RAM and CPU targets ensure the overlay is unobtrusive alongside resource-heavy applications like IDEs and browsers.

