| FR-BR-04 | The browser MUST provide Back, Forward, Refresh, and Stop buttons | P0 | Standard navigation behavior |
| FR-BR-05 | The browser MUST support opening a new tab via button and Ctrl+T | P0 | New tab opens with a configurable home page or blank page |
| FR-BR-06 | The browser MUST support closing a tab via button and Ctrl+W | P0 | Closing last tab does not close the application; shows new tab page |
| FR-BR-07 | The browser MUST persist cookies, local storage, IndexedDB, and session storage across application restarts | P0 | User remains logged into ChatGPT, Google, etc. after restart |
| FR-BR-08 | The browser MUST support file downloads with a configurable download directory | P1 | Download progress shown; completed files accessible from the downloads panel |
| FR-BR-09 | The browser MUST support file uploads via `<input type="file">` and drag-and-drop | P1 | Users can upload files to Google Docs, ChatGPT, etc. |
| FR-BR-10 | The browser MUST render PDFs inline | P1 | PDF viewer with zoom, page navigation, and scroll |
| FR-BR-11 | The browser MUST support bookmarks (add, remove, rename, organize in folders) | P1 | Bookmarks persist across sessions; accessible from a bookmarks panel |
| FR-BR-12 | The browser MUST support Find-in-Page (Ctrl+F) | P1 | Highlights matches; navigates between them |
| FR-BR-13 | The browser MUST support zoom per tab (Ctrl+Plus, Ctrl+Minus, Ctrl+0) | P1 | Zoom level persists per tab within the session |
| FR-BR-14 | The browser MUST load the following sites without functional regressions: ChatGPT, Claude, Gemini, Google Docs, Google Sheets, Notion, GitHub, StackOverflow | P0 | Manual QA pass for each site; login, navigation, and core features work |
| FR-BR-15 | The browser MUST support JavaScript ES2020+ | P0 | Modern web applications function correctly |
| FR-BR-16 | The browser MUST support WebSocket connections (required by ChatGPT, Claude) | P0 | Real-time responses stream correctly |
| FR-BR-17 | The browser MUST isolate browser profile data within the portable `data/` directory | P0 | No data written to the user's default Chrome/Edge profile |
| FR-BR-18 | The browser MUST support a "Copy Selected Text to Smart Clipboard" context menu action | P0 | Right-click → "Copy to Smart Clipboard" adds selection to the clipboard panel |
| FR-BR-19 | The browser MUST support DevTools (toggleable, off by default) for debugging | P2 | F12 or menu toggle opens DevTools |

### Design Rationale
Qt WebEngine (Chromium-based) is recommended over CEF because it integrates natively with the PySide6 widget tree, reducing interop complexity. Session persistence is critical — users will not tolerate re-logging into ChatGPT every launch. WebSocket support is non-negotiable for streaming AI responses.

