## 7.3 Module 3: Workspace Management

### Purpose
Isolate user contexts so that different projects, workshops, classes, or clients do not interfere with each other.

| Req ID | Requirement | Priority | Acceptance Criteria |
|---|---|---|---|
| FR-WS-01 | The application MUST support creating named workspaces | P0 | User provides a name; workspace is created with default settings |
| FR-WS-02 | Each workspace MUST independently store: browser tabs (URLs + history), clipboard entries, typing settings, window geometry (size, position, opacity), and user preferences | P0 | Switching workspaces restores all saved state |
| FR-WS-03 | The application MUST support switching between workspaces in < 1 second | P0 | Measured from click to interactive UI in the target workspace |
| FR-WS-04 | The application MUST support duplicating a workspace (deep copy) | P1 | All state including clipboard entries is copied; new workspace has a unique name |
| FR-WS-05 | The application MUST support renaming a workspace | P0 | Name updates in the UI and on disk |
| FR-WS-06 | The application MUST support deleting a workspace with confirmation | P0 | Confirmation dialog; data is permanently removed |
| FR-WS-07 | The application MUST support exporting a workspace to a `.bmw` archive file | P2 | Archive contains all workspace data in a portable format |
| FR-WS-08 | The application MUST support importing a workspace from a `.bmw` file | P2 | Validates archive integrity before import; reports errors |
| FR-WS-09 | The application MUST persist at least one "Default" workspace that cannot be deleted | P0 | Delete action is disabled for the Default workspace |
| FR-WS-10 | The application MUST display the active workspace name in the title bar and status bar | P0 | Name is always visible |

### Workspace Data Model

```
workspace/
├── meta.json              # name, created_at, updated_at, settings
├── browser/
│   ├── profile/           # Chromium profile (cookies, storage, cache)
│   └── session.json       # open tabs, tab order, active tab, per-tab zoom
├── clipboard/
│   └── entries.db         # SQLite database of clipboard entries
├── typing/
│   └── settings.json      # speed, queue, preferences
└── window/
    └── geometry.json       # x, y, width, height, opacity, collapsed, pinned
```

### Design Rationale
Workspaces are the organizational backbone. Deep isolation (including separate Chromium profiles) ensures that a teacher's classroom workspace doesn't leak cookies into their personal workspace. The `.bmw` export format enables sharing curated setups between colleagues.

> [!NOTE]
> Separate Chromium profiles per workspace will increase disk usage. Each profile starts at ~20 MB and grows with cache. A "Shared Browser Profile" option may be offered in settings as a space-saving alternative (deferred to v1.1).

