## 9.3 Interaction Flows

### Flow 1: Copy and Type Workflow
1. User browses to ChatGPT in the embedded browser.
2. User selects text from a ChatGPT response.
3. User right-clicks → "Copy to Smart Clipboard" (or presses Ctrl+Shift+C).
4. Text appears in the Clipboard panel with a green flash animation.
5. User clicks the sidebar 📋 icon to view the clipboard.
6. User hovers over the entry → "Type This" button appears.
7. User clicks "Type This."
8. A 3-second countdown begins ("Typing starts in 3… 2… 1…").
9. User clicks on the target application (e.g., VS Code).
10. Typing begins at the configured speed.
11. Progress bar updates in the batmanoverlay status bar.
12. User presses Ctrl+Shift+P to pause; presses again to resume.
13. Typing completes; status bar shows "Typing complete ✓" for 5 seconds.

### Flow 2: Workspace Switch
1. User clicks the workspace name in the title bar.
2. A dropdown shows all workspaces with icons and last-used timestamps.
3. User selects a different workspace.
4. The UI transitions (slide animation, 200 ms).
5. Browser tabs, clipboard, and settings reflect the new workspace.

### Flow 3: Global Search
1. User presses Ctrl+Shift+F.
2. A centered modal with a search input appears (Spotlight-style).
3. User types a query.
4. Results appear grouped by type (Clipboard, Bookmarks, Tabs, History, Workspaces).
5. User navigates results with arrow keys; presses Enter.
6. The relevant panel opens with the selected item highlighted.

