# 13. Database Design

## 13.1 Storage Strategy Decision

| Strategy | Pros | Cons | Verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| **SQLite for structured data + JSON for configuration** (Hybrid) | Best of both worlds: SQLite handles large datasets and search; JSON handles human-readable config files | Two storage technologies to maintain | ✅ **Selected** |
| SQLite for everything | Unified storage; powerful queries | Configuration files are harder to manually edit/debug; overhead for small datasets | ❌ |
| JSON for everything | Simple; human-readable; portable | Slow for large datasets; no indexing; no full-text search; no concurrency control | ❌ |

**Justification:** The hybrid approach uses each technology where it excels. SQLite with FTS5 provides sub-200ms full-text search across 10,000+ clipboard entries — impossible with JSON file scanning. JSON files are used for configuration (settings, geometry, metadata) because they are small, human-readable, and benefit from easy manual editing during development and debugging.

## 13.2 SQLite Schema

### Database: `data/workspaces/<workspace>/clipboard/entries.db`

```sql
-- Enable WAL mode for concurrent read/write
PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL;
PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON;

-- Clipboard entries
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS clipboard_entries (
    id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,   -- UUID
    text        TEXT NOT NULL,
    source_url  TEXT,
    source_title TEXT,
    note        TEXT,
    is_pinned   INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,  -- 0 or 1
    char_count  INTEGER NOT NULL,
    created_at  TEXT NOT NULL,      -- ISO 8601
    updated_at  TEXT NOT NULL       -- ISO 8601
);

-- Categories (tags)
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS categories (
    id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,   -- UUID
    name        TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE,
    color       TEXT,               -- Hex color code
    created_at  TEXT NOT NULL
);

-- Many-to-many: entries ↔ categories
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS entry_categories (
    entry_id    TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES clipboard_entries(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    category_id TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES categories(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    PRIMARY KEY (entry_id, category_id)
);

-- Full-text search index
CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS clipboard_fts USING fts5(
    text,
    note,
    source_title,
    content='clipboard_entries',
    content_rowid='rowid'
);

-- Triggers to keep FTS index in sync
CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS clipboard_entries_ai AFTER INSERT ON clipboard_entries BEGIN
    INSERT INTO clipboard_fts(rowid, text, note, source_title)
    VALUES (new.rowid, new.text, new.note, new.source_title);
END;

CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS clipboard_entries_ad AFTER DELETE ON clipboard_entries BEGIN
    INSERT INTO clipboard_fts(clipboard_fts, rowid, text, note, source_title)
    VALUES ('delete', old.rowid, old.text, old.note, old.source_title);
END;

CREATE TRIGGER IF NOT EXISTS clipboard_entries_au AFTER UPDATE ON clipboard_entries BEGIN
    INSERT INTO clipboard_fts(clipboard_fts, rowid, text, note, source_title)
    VALUES ('delete', old.rowid, old.text, old.note, old.source_title);
    INSERT INTO clipboard_fts(rowid, text, note, source_title)
    VALUES (new.rowid, new.text, new.note, new.source_title);
END;

-- Indexes
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_entries_pinned ON clipboard_entries(is_pinned);
CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_entries_created ON clipboard_entries(created_at);
```

### Database: `data/workspaces/<workspace>/browser/bookmarks.db`

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bookmarks (
    id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,   -- UUID
    title       TEXT NOT NULL,
    url         TEXT NOT NULL,
    folder_id   TEXT REFERENCES bookmark_folders(id) ON DELETE SET NULL,
    created_at  TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS bookmark_folders (
    id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    name        TEXT NOT NULL,
    parent_id   TEXT REFERENCES bookmark_folders(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    created_at  TEXT NOT NULL
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_bookmarks_folder ON bookmarks(folder_id);
```

### Database: `data/workspaces/<workspace>/browser/history.db`

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS browser_history (
    id          TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
    url         TEXT NOT NULL,
    title       TEXT,
    visit_time  TEXT NOT NULL,      -- ISO 8601
    visit_count INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 1
);

CREATE VIRTUAL TABLE IF NOT EXISTS history_fts USING fts5(
    url, title,
    content='browser_history',
    content_rowid='rowid'
);

CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_history_time ON browser_history(visit_time);
```

