# 17. Accessibility

## 17.1 Standards Compliance

The application targets **WCAG 2.1 Level AA** adapted for desktop applications, following the [W3C User Agent Accessibility Guidelines (UAAG)](https://www.w3.org/TR/UAAG20/) and Qt's built-in accessibility framework.

## 17.2 Implementation Checklist

| Category | Requirement | Implementation |
|---|---|---|
| **Keyboard** | All controls reachable via Tab/Shift+Tab | Set `tabOrder()` on all widgets; verify no dead ends |
| **Keyboard** | Activatable via Enter/Space | Default Qt behavior for buttons; custom handlers for cards |
| **Keyboard** | Escape closes dialogs and modals | Connect `Escape` key to `close()` on all dialogs |
| **Focus** | Visible focus indicator on all interactive elements | 2px solid `--accent` outline; high-contrast override |
| **Focus** | Logical focus order (top-to-bottom, left-to-right) | Manual `setTabOrder()` chain |
| **Screen Reader** | All widgets expose `accessibleName` and `accessibleDescription` | Set via `QWidget.setAccessibleName()` |
| **Screen Reader** | Dynamic content changes announced | Use `QAccessible::updateAccessibility()` for state changes |
| **Screen Reader** | Tested with NVDA and JAWS | QA checklist item |
| **Color** | Minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio | Verified for both themes using contrast checker |
| **Color** | Not sole information carrier | Icons + text accompany all color indicators |
| **Motion** | Animations disableable | Settings toggle; also respects `prefers-reduced-motion` via `QStyleHints` |
| **Scaling** | UI scales 80%–200% | Relative sizing; no hardcoded pixel values for text |
| **Scaling** | Respects system DPI | Qt handles DPI scaling; verify no clipping at 150%, 200% |
| **High Contrast** | Supports Windows High Contrast mode | Detect via `QPalette`; apply high-contrast stylesheet |
