# 22. Risks

| ID | Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| R-01 | Qt WebEngine binary size makes distribution too large (> 300 MB) | High | Medium | Accept the trade-off; document download size; explore UPX compression for non-Chromium DLLs |
| R-02 | Website compatibility issues (ChatGPT, Claude) due to user-agent or feature detection | Medium | High | Match Chrome's user-agent string; test monthly; maintain a compatibility matrix |
| R-03 | Antivirus false positives (PyInstaller executables are frequently flagged) | High | High | Code signing (§21.5); submit to major AV vendors for whitelisting; transparent process name |
| R-04 | SendInput blocked by UAC or Group Policy in corporate environments | Medium | Medium | Document limitation; provide fallback using `pyperclip` + "Paste" instruction |
| R-05 | Qt WebEngine Chromium version lags behind, causing website breakage | Medium | High | Pin PySide6 to recent releases; test quarterly; document minimum Qt version |
| R-06 | High memory usage with many browser tabs | High | Medium | Tab suspension after idle period; document recommended tab count (≤10) |
| R-07 | Chromium profile data consumes excessive disk space | Medium | Low | Configurable cache size; "Clear Browser Data" in settings |
| R-08 | Users misuse the product for cheating despite explicit non-goals | Low | High | Clear documentation, ToS, and ethical use policy; no stealth features exist |
| R-09 | Python GIL causes UI stuttering during heavy clipboard operations | Low | Medium | Offload database writes to `QThreadPool`; use WAL mode |
| R-10 | PySide6 LGPL license compliance | Low | High | Do not modify PySide6 source; dynamically link (default); document license in About |

