# 26. Appendix

## A. Glossary

| Term | Definition |
|---|---|
| **batmanoverlay** | The product name. A portable Windows desktop productivity and presentation assistant. |
| **Smart Clipboard** | The application's persistent, searchable clipboard that stores text copied from the embedded browser. |
| **Typing Engine** | The module that simulates keyboard input character-by-character into a target application window. |
| **Workspace** | An isolated context containing browser tabs, clipboard entries, typing settings, and window geometry. |
| **SendInput** | A Windows API function for synthesizing keyboard and mouse input events. |
| **RegisterHotKey** | A Windows API function for registering system-wide keyboard shortcuts. |
| **FTS5** | SQLite's Full-Text Search extension, version 5. Provides fast full-text search indexing. |
| **WAL** | Write-Ahead Logging. An SQLite journal mode that improves concurrent read/write performance. |
| **Qt WebEngine** | Qt's Chromium-based browser engine, used for embedding web content in Qt applications. |
| **PySide6** | The official Python binding for the Qt 6 framework, maintained by the Qt Company. |
| **.bmw** | batmanoverlay Workspace file format. A ZIP archive containing all workspace data for export/import. |
| **PyInstaller** | A tool for packaging Python applications into standalone executables. |
| **DPAPI** | Windows Data Protection API. Used by Chromium to encrypt stored credentials. |

